# Profile: zagros (zagros sandbox goatnet — per-uuid slot-pool fabric).
#
# Concrete fallback values for standing a partner moon-pod up against the live zagros fabric. zagros
# is a SANDBOX (not the production shape): enrollment is netbird setup-key based and the Zenoh
# write namespace is a per-uuid SLOT (not release/<partner>). None of this is canon; production
# deltas come from the production profile + the signed bundle (see docs/zagros-vs-production.md).
#
# The partner's bundle is minted by machine enrollment: the org's custodian runs
# `goat machine enroll <handle> --node-class <class>` against a goat-seeded quota, which mints
# the slot, the mTLS identity, and a single-use netbird setup-key in one act. The BUNDLE is the
# source of truth: first-boot reads the router endpoint and the mTLS identity straight from it.
# The values below are only fallbacks for hand-driven validation when a field is absent from
# the bundle.

# --- Mesh client ---
# zagros does not run a silent control plane on the sandbox; enrollment is a netbird setup-key, so
# the cleaner partner on-ramp is netbird-only.
GOAT_CLIENT_MODE=netbird-only

# --- Zenoh ---
# Endpoint the pod's router dials. The bundle's router_endpoint WINS when present; this is only
# the fallback for hand-driven validation. The fabric router's cert SAN binds its mesh address,
# not this DNS name, so the rendered config sets verify_name_on_connect: false
# (host/zenoh-router.json5.tmpl) — turning it on fails the handshake.
ZENOH_FABRIC_ENDPOINT=tls/zenoh.zagros.netbird.zagros.example:7447
ZENOH_LOCAL_ENDPOINT=tls/127.0.0.1:7447
# Transport is chosen by the endpoint SCHEME — nothing else changes (same mTLS
# identity, same ACL). The zagros sandbox also runs a QUIC listener on UDP :7448;
# to dial QUIC instead of TLS/TCP, use the quic/ scheme + :7448. QUIC helps on a
# lossy/mobile edge (no head-of-line blocking, connection migration); TLS is the
# default. Know both — see docs/transport-tls-vs-quic.md + examples/transport_quic.py.
# ZENOH_FABRIC_ENDPOINT_QUIC=quic/zenoh.zagros.netbird.zagros.example:7448

# ACL subject identity axis (informational — the axis is baked into the router ACL template,
# nothing reads a variable for it). On the zagros sandbox the cert CN, the portal prefix, and the
# write namespace are ALL the uuid slot anchor (slot_id); the baked ACL keys write rules off the
# cert CN, so the axis is cert_common_names. The pod's cert CN itself arrives in the bundle —
# there is no CN field to fill here.

# --- Namespace ---
# zagros write namespace is the per-uuid slot anchor: the pod may only write <slot_id>/**. There is
# no release/<partner>/ grant on the sandbox; a publish outside <slot_id>/ is silently denied.
# Set this to the slot_id from your onboarding response (minted at enrollment).
PARTNER_NAMESPACE=CHANGE-ME-zagros-uuid-slot
# Bilateral inbound prefix the fabric publishes TO the pod. On the sandbox there is no separate
# bilateral grant yet, so this defaults to the pod's own slot (first-boot falls back to
# PARTNER_NAMESPACE when unset). Set it only once a bilateral inbound channel is granted.
# INBOUND_NAMESPACE=

# --- Pod identity ---
# Stable id for THIS pod: compose passes it to the audit-sink as AUDIT_SUBSCRIBER_ID and it
# labels the metrics. Defaults to "moon-pod" when unset — set it (the machine handle works)
# when more than one pod reports metrics.
# POD_ID=

# --- Audit ---
# v0 runs the audit-sink OBSERVE-ONLY: nothing persists durably, so there is no retention knob
# to set here. Durable local audit (and the partner-contract retention requirement) is a
# documented follow-up — see docs/architecture.md "Audit".

# --- PKI ---
# Fabric-TLS CA trust comes from the bundle (ca_roots); the root that verifies the bundle itself is
# added with `goat ca add` (docs/partner-run-guide.md, "Trust your goatnet's CA root"). Neither is
# compiled in.
